Welcome to the sourcecode of Reaction 1.0.   Reaction uses a modified version of the ioquake3 engine and as such much of the ioquake3 documentation also covers Reaction.

Reaction builds with CMake 3.25 or newer and a C compiler, like ioquake3. From the directory containing this readme:

    cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
    cmake --build build

The client (Reaction), the dedicated server (Reactionded), both renderers and the game modules land in build/Release, the
game modules as libraries in Boomstick/ and as QVMs in Boomstick/vm/. The QVM tools (q3lcc, q3asm) are built on the way
with the host compiler. CMake options choose what is built (cmake -LH build lists them). Keep BUILD_RENDERER_GL2 on: many
maps, the UI and more depend on features of the new renderer.

Windows: tested with MinGW-w64 (GCC 13.2) and Ninja on Windows 11. Put MinGW and Ninja on PATH and add -G Ninja to the
first command. Visual Studio builds are untested; CMake can generate the project files (-G).

Linux and macOS: the same commands follow ioquake3's CMake build but are untested for Reaction.

